      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 11,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "text": ".gsd_transform_hyp()  — run once per hypothesis\n  1. .gsd_looks() → looks (analyses with data) and\n     maturity (first look at full information)\n  2. Only one look, at full info?\n       → repeated p = raw p, copied into all later looks\n     Otherwise:\n       a. .gsd_boundary_table(): for a log grid of levels\n          from 1e-14 to alpha, call gsDesign::gsBound1()\n          once per level → boundary at every look\n       b. .gsd_check_well_ordered(): boundaries must rise\n          with level, else abort\n       c. .gsd_invert() per look: log-log interpolate to\n          find the level whose boundary equals the raw p\n       d. After maturity, copy the maturity value forward\n  3. If look_back[i]: running pmin across looks",
      "originalText": ".gsd_transform_hyp()  — run once per hypothesis\n  1. .gsd_looks() → looks (analyses with data) and\n     maturity (first look at full information)\n  2. Only one look, at full info?\n       → repeated p = raw p, copied into all later looks\n     Otherwise:\n       a. .gsd_boundary_table(): for a log grid of levels\n          from 1e-14 to alpha, call gsDesign::gsBound1()\n          once per level → boundary at every look\n       b. .gsd_check_well_ordered(): boundaries must rise\n          with level, else abort\n       c. .gsd_invert() per look: log-log interpolate to\n          find the level whose boundary equals the raw p\n       d. After maturity, copy the maturity value forward\n  3. If look_back[i]: running pmin across looks",
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "n--tf_hyp",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": false,
      "index": "ag"
    },
